{# roomhive/host/quit_hosting.html.twig
   Host › Quit Hosting — 1:1 port of legacy host/quithosting.php.

   Host dashboard shell (extends host/base.html.twig; sidebar
   Settings › "Quit Hosting" highlights via
   active_nav = 'quithosting' — the sidebar's RED link to
   /host/quit-hosting was pre-reserved by the shell; legacy
   note: $activePage = 'quithosting' matches host_sidebar.php's
   settings-group key).

   SHELL NOTE (legacy "SHELL FIX" repaired three pieces): the
   ported shell ships all three — shared navbar with bell +
   notification dropdown, the REAL host sidebar (legacy's old
   /includes/hostsidebar.php path silently rendered NO sidebar
   through an is_file guard), and the footer. Legacy also
   wrapped the card in its own .qh-layout because the page
   predated the shell standardization; the port drops that
   wrapper (the shell's .host-layout replaces it) and keeps the
   .qh-card + inner qh-* CSS VERBATIM.

   Content (1:1 with legacy):
   - Red "Quit Hosting" h1 (#a1332e) + the keep-your-stuff
     paragraph + the 3-item qh-list (listings unlisted
     immediately, bookings stay on record, become a host again
     anytime)
   - INLINE error list (.qh-error, one <p> per error) — NOT
     PRG: legacy re-renders the page on failure (same pattern
     as the Edit Profile port); only SUCCESS redirects
   - The quit form: Password + "Type QUIT to confirm" fields,
     full-width red QUIT HOSTING button, qh_csrf hidden field,
     and the KEPT onsubmit confirm() dialog (verbatim text)
   - Cancel link "Cancel — keep hosting" → /host/profile
     (legacy hostprofile.php)

   ON SUCCESS the controller:
     1. UPDATE users SET is_host = 0 (transaction)
     2. UPDATE listings SET status = 'unlisted' WHERE user_id
        (transaction — legacy FIXED note #1: the real column is
        user_id, not host_id)
     3. commit → clear the is_host session flag → redirect
        /profile?quit_hosting=1 (legacy
        /webprogg/user/userprofile.php?quit_hosting=1; the
        ported profile page is /profile — it does not consume
        the flag yet, same policy as stored legacy links
        awaiting their page port)

   ICONS: this page has none in legacy (no data-lucide
   anywhere) — the port carries no icons either.

   CSS NOTE: qh-* styles were self-contained in the legacy
   page (its own <style> block) — redeclared page-locally with
   the same values, plus dark-mode overrides consistent with
   the shell (legacy had none for the card).

   Pairs with: HostQuitHostingController
     GET|POST /host/quit-hosting   name app_host_quit_hosting
#}
{% extends 'host/base.html.twig' %}

{% set active_nav = 'quithosting' %}

{% block page_title %}Quit Hosting — RoomHive{% endblock %}

{% block styles %}
<style>
    /* =========================================================
       QUIT CARD — qh-* verbatim from the legacy page's own
       <style> block (self-contained so the card renders
       regardless of host CSS — legacy comment kept). The
       .qh-layout / .qh-main wrapper CSS is dropped: the shell's
       .host-layout / .host-content replace it.
    ========================================================= */
    .qh-card {
        background: #ffffff;
        border: 1px solid rgba(28, 42, 56, 0.08);
        border-radius: 16px;
        box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(28, 42, 56, 0.10);
        padding: 28px;
        max-width: 640px;
    }

    .qh-card h1 {
        margin: 0 0 10px;
        color: #a1332e;
        font-size: 22px;
        font-weight: 800;
    }

    .qh-card>p {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-size: 13.5px;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: #5d6875;
    }

    .qh-list {
        margin: 0 0 18px;
        padding-left: 18px;
        font-size: 13.5px;
        line-height: 1.8;
        color: #5d6875;
    }

    .qh-field {
        margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .qh-field label {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 6px;
        font-size: 12.5px;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #1c2a38;
    }

    .qh-field input {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 11px 12px;
        border: 1px solid #d9dee4;
        border-radius: 10px;
        font: inherit;
        font-size: 14px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .qh-field input:focus {
        outline: none;
        border-color: #b07708;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(176, 119, 8, 0.15);
    }

    .qh-error {
        background: #fdecea;
        border: 1px solid #f5c6c2;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 10px 14px;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        font-size: 13.5px;
    }

    .qh-error p {
        margin: 0 0 4px;
        color: #b3261e;
    }

    .qh-btn {
        width: 100%;
        background: #e0524d;
        color: #ffffff;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 12px;
        font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 13px;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: background 0.2s ease;
    }

    .qh-btn:hover {
        background: #c84642;
    }

    .qh-cancel {
        display: block;
        text-align: center;
        margin-top: 14px;
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #1c2a38;
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .qh-cancel:hover {
        color: #b07708;
    }

    /* ---- Dark mode (shell-consistent; legacy had none for the card) ---- */
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-card {
        background: #141b24;
        border-color: #1a222b;
        box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-card>p,
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-list { color: #8d99a5; }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-card h1 { color: #f28b82; }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-field label { color: #e8ecf1; }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-field input {
        background: #141b24;
        border-color: #2a3540;
        color: #e8ecf1;
    }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-field input:focus {
        border-color: #f6c04e;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(246, 192, 78, 0.18);
    }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-error {
        background: rgba(226, 74, 61, 0.15);
        border-color: rgba(226, 74, 61, 0.4);
    }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-error p { color: #f28b82; }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-cancel { color: #e8ecf1; }
    body[data-theme="dark"] .qh-cancel:hover { color: #f6c04e; }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .qh-btn { transition: none; }
    }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<div class="qh-card">

    <h1>Quit Hosting</h1>

    <p>
        This turns your RoomHive account back into a regular guest account.
        <strong>You keep your account, bookings history, and reviews</strong> —
        you just stop being a host.
    </p>

    <ul class="qh-list">
        <li>All of your listings will be unlisted immediately.</li>
        <li>Existing bookings stay on record for you and your guests.</li>
        <li>You can become a host again anytime from the Become a Host page.</li>
    </ul>

    {% if errors %}
        <div class="qh-error">
            {% for error in errors %}
                <p>{{ error }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <form method="POST" action="{{ path('app_host_quit_hosting') }}"
        onsubmit="return confirm('This will end your hosting on RoomHive and unlist all your listings. Continue?');">

        <input type="hidden" name="qh_csrf" value="{{ qh_csrf }}">

        <div class="qh-field">
            <label for="qhPw">Password</label>
            <input type="password" id="qhPw" name="quit_password" required>
        </div>

        <div class="qh-field">
            <label for="qhWord">Type QUIT to confirm</label>
            <input type="text" id="qhWord" name="confirm_word" required>
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="qh-btn">QUIT HOSTING</button>
    </form>

    <a href="/host/profile" class="qh-cancel">Cancel — keep hosting</a>

</div>

{% endblock %}
